The theorem preserves the exact existing zero-defect result while exposing its
domain:

```text
Phi=0:
    Hess V = D Phi^* D Phi;

Phi!=0 and critical:
    Hess V = D Phi^* D Phi + residual curvature.
```

It therefore suggests, but does not yet establish, the following separation:

```text
exact q79 closure endpoint  -> reference vacuum/background;
nonzero sector minimum      -> persistent defect candidate;
K                           -> reversible phase transport;
Gamma                       -> repair/damping;
full residual Hessian       -> local stability.
```

This does not close `B.ACTION.01`. The selected physical source must still
